WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.241 --> 00:00:02.991
(dramatic music)

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.587
- [Narrator] Known as
the land of fire and ice,

00:00:09.587 --> 00:00:12.953
Iceland is an island of
extremes, where people wage

00:00:12.953 --> 00:00:15.903
a relentless war against the elements.

00:00:15.903 --> 00:00:18.561
- It's seriously unpredictable weather.

00:00:18.561 --> 00:00:22.122
It's basically like a
battle storm of different

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:24.510
high pressure, low pressure areas.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.177
Anything can happen.

00:00:27.305 --> 00:00:29.261
- [Narrator] Dangerous
conditions mean people can find

00:00:29.261 --> 00:00:33.658
themselves in serious trouble,
and in need of rescue.

00:00:33.658 --> 00:00:35.437
But there's a problem.

00:00:35.437 --> 00:00:39.373
The small country has no army
or government program to help,

00:00:39.373 --> 00:00:42.450
so citizens formed the Icelandic
Search and Rescue Team,

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:46.200
known as ICE-SAR, a
national emergency force.

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:50.716
They're everyday people,
willing to risk their lives

00:00:50.716 --> 00:00:54.698
to save others in the worst
conditions imaginable.

00:00:54.698 --> 00:00:57.937
- You're going out in the
conditions when everyone else

00:00:57.937 --> 00:00:59.702
is supposed to be inside.

00:00:59.702 --> 00:01:03.869
So we have to be a little
bit crazy, but in a good way.

00:01:09.374 --> 00:01:12.544
- ICE-SAR is a community
of volunteers that responds

00:01:12.544 --> 00:01:15.961
to calls for help all year round in Iceland.

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:19.693
I think to take part in ICE-SAR,
you just have to be willing

00:01:19.693 --> 00:01:22.673
to put forward the skills that you have.

00:01:22.673 --> 00:01:26.284
I sometimes consider a
rescue team like a village.

00:01:26.284 --> 00:01:30.179
You need every kind of person
to make everything work.

00:01:30.179 --> 00:01:35.055
- I think it's kind of amazing,
because it's all volunteers.

00:01:35.055 --> 00:01:39.928
We have professors, taxi
drivers, carpenters, plumbers,

00:01:39.928 --> 00:01:44.095
office workers, just name it,
men and women, all kind of people.

00:01:45.916 --> 00:01:50.136
It's very hard to imagine
Iceland without our association

00:01:50.136 --> 00:01:51.136
of go teams.

00:01:53.761 --> 00:01:56.761
(people chattering)

00:01:58.996 --> 00:02:02.372
(upbeat music)

00:02:02.372 --> 00:02:04.461
- [Narrator] Iceland's
breathtaking landscape attracts

00:02:04.461 --> 00:02:08.824
tourists and adventure seekers
from all over the world, but

00:02:08.824 --> 00:02:12.532
that beauty can lure people
to a false sense of security.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:15.075
- The weather conditions can change

00:02:15.075 --> 00:02:17.368
faster than anything else.

00:02:17.368 --> 00:02:22.188
You can have a sunny day, and
in two minutes, it's a storm.

00:02:22.188 --> 00:02:25.521
Wind, rain, even snow in the summertime.

00:02:27.108 --> 00:02:30.089
- People are just going for
a hike, and they're pretty

00:02:30.089 --> 00:02:32.315
confident that the
mountain they're going on

00:02:32.315 --> 00:02:33.732
is not dangerous.

00:02:35.675 --> 00:02:37.777
We have the lower
glaciers, which have become

00:02:37.777 --> 00:02:40.444
quite a popular tourist
attraction, and people are going

00:02:40.444 --> 00:02:43.494
for walks on these, and
they are full of crevasses,

00:02:43.494 --> 00:02:47.639
extremely dangerous, super
slippery, and then they fall over

00:02:47.639 --> 00:02:50.434
and hurt themselves,
then they have to rely on

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:53.767
Search and Rescue to come and find them.

00:02:54.637 --> 00:02:56.480
- [Narrator] For average
citizens to gain the skills

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.716
needed to be part of ICE-SAR,
they go through a rigorous

00:02:59.716 --> 00:03:01.899
18-month training program.

00:03:01.899 --> 00:03:05.941
They learn mountaineering,
climbing and orienteering.

00:03:05.941 --> 00:03:10.167
It takes a huge skill set,
but when you can deal with

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:14.250
any weather, then you can
go out and help people.

00:03:19.262 --> 00:03:23.308
- Across the whole country,
I think, our teams get to 4.5

00:03:23.308 --> 00:03:24.475
callers per day.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:29.472
And our people, they're
running from their own work

00:03:29.472 --> 00:03:32.222
or their family to join the team.

00:03:34.343 --> 00:03:37.826
- When I get called out,
we have three codes.

00:03:37.826 --> 00:03:40.576
F1, high priority, life at stake.

00:03:41.627 --> 00:03:43.710
F2, not as high priority.

00:03:44.553 --> 00:03:46.053
And F3, easygoing.

00:03:47.496 --> 00:03:51.049
When you get called out high
priority, and you get your text

00:03:51.049 --> 00:03:54.717
and it says a child, and your
heart goes pounding almost

00:03:54.717 --> 00:03:57.759
out of your chest, and you run
out, I don't even say goodbye

00:03:57.759 --> 00:03:59.926
to my children or my wife.

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:05.419
I can remember one call,
a boy, lost in (unclear).

00:04:05.419 --> 00:04:08.098
All I could think about was my son.

00:04:08.098 --> 00:04:11.801
If he got lost, I would like
to have everyone helping.

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:15.238
So a lot of emotions comes
up when you get called up.

00:04:15.238 --> 00:04:17.029
(muffled voice on radio)

00:04:17.029 --> 00:04:19.481
(melodic piano playing)

00:04:19.481 --> 00:04:23.466
- I'm proud of the unity
and the fight that people

00:04:23.466 --> 00:04:27.633
are willing to sacrifice in
their spare time to help others.

00:04:29.921 --> 00:04:33.358
- The feeling that I get
when we rescue someone.

00:04:33.358 --> 00:04:35.703
It doesn't have to be me
that finds the person.

00:04:35.703 --> 00:04:38.977
It can be another group
searching somewhere else,

00:04:38.977 --> 00:04:40.707
but we're searching for the same person.

00:04:40.707 --> 00:04:44.596
When someone gets found, we
get this wellness feeling.

00:04:44.596 --> 00:04:47.209
We did something right.

00:04:47.209 --> 00:04:50.692
- They're our heroes in so
many ways, but in Icelandic

00:04:50.692 --> 00:04:54.743
culture, we don't do
a lot of hero talk.

00:04:54.743 --> 00:04:56.051
- No, I'm not a hero.

00:04:56.051 --> 00:04:58.218
I'm just a part of a team.

00:04:59.535 --> 00:05:01.370
- I'm not a hero, no.

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:03.453
I'm just a normal person.

00:05:04.446 --> 00:05:06.463
- I'm very proud of the Association

00:05:06.463 --> 00:05:09.142
and what they have accomplished.

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:11.559
They've saved a lot of lives.

